course: dictionary
lesson: 13135
title: Foraging: searching for food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Foraging means searching for food, especially wild food. «The squirrels were foraging for acorns under the oak tree.» Squirrels are looking for food in the wild, so foraging must mean searching for food. Always check: does the meaning fit the sentence?
explain: People can go foraging too. «On Sunday we went foraging for blackberries in the lane.» Foraging can be a hobby, but a wild plant or mushroom is only safe to eat if an expert adult says so.
explain: The word can also be informal. «Tom was foraging in the cupboard for biscuits.» Tom is not hunting for wild food here. He is searching around for something, so foraging can mean searching around, too.
fact: Foraging means searching for food, especially wild food.
fact: «Foraging» is the -ing form of the verb «forage», so you can also say «forage», «forages» and «foraged».
fact: Bees are foraging when they fly from flower to flower to collect nectar.
fact: Foraging for wild food is a hobby, but never eat a wild plant or mushroom unless an expert adult says it is safe.
fact: Informally, «foraging» can mean searching around for something, like «foraging in the cupboard».
exercise: «The hedgehog was foraging for beetles in the leaves.» What is the hedgehog doing? | Building a nest | Swimming in a pond | *Searching for food | Sleeping under the leaves
exercise: «Dad and I go foraging for blackberries every autumn.» What does foraging mean here? | Cooking a big dinner at home | *Collecting wild food like berries as a hobby | Planting a new garden | Buying fruit at the shop
exercise: «The ants were busy foraging for crumbs.» Find and copy the word that means searching for food. | crumbs | *foraging | busy | ants
test: «Ella was foraging in her bag for a pencil.» What is Ella doing? | *Searching around for something | Singing a song | Sleeping on the bus | Writing a story
test: Mum says, «Never eat a mushroom you find unless an expert says it is safe.» Why? | Mushrooms are always too big to eat | Mushrooms can only be eaten raw | *Some wild mushrooms are poisonous | Mushrooms only grow in summer
exam: «Squirrels spend autumn foraging for nuts to store for winter.» What does foraging mean in this sentence? | Climbing tall trees to sleep | Hiding from the winter cold | *Searching for food | Making a warm nest
